Revert "Switch to Gazpacho/2026.1 sources".

This reverts the OPENSTACK_RELEASE bump from kolla commit 352b7fce
("Switch to Gazpacho/2026.1 sources", 2026-03-18). The stable/2026.1
branch has since been cut across the OpenStack ecosystem and master
is now doing post-Gazpacho development, so the late-cycle pin to
'2026.1' is stale and needs to be reverted back to 'master' --
mirroring the same housekeeping pattern as the 2025.1->master
revert (87678d014, 2025-05) and the 2025.2->master revert
(c30e4e524, 2025-12).

Concrete symptom: Nova master commit 770580bb (2026-05-29) bumped
oslo.privsep in requirements.txt from >=2.6.2 to >=3.11.0. With
OPENSTACK_RELEASE = '2026.1', openstack_branch resolves to
stable-2026.1 and openstack-base pulls
requirements-stable-2026.1.tar.gz, which still pins
oslo.privsep===3.10.1. The resulting ResolutionImpossible blows
up nova-base image builds. Reverting to 'master' makes
openstack_branch == 'master' and pulls requirements-master.tar.gz,
which already has the matching oslo.privsep===3.11.0 pin.

OPENSTACK_RELEASE_CODENAME stays 'Gazpacho' here, matching the
precedent set by both prior reverts -- the codename is updated
as part of the next "Switch to <codename>/<release> sources"
flip, not on the revert.

Prompt: The patch I asked you to draft earlier (a surgical
sources.py override pinning openstack-base to
requirements-master.tar.gz) was over-cautious. The actually
correct fix is to revert OPENSTACK_RELEASE back to 'master',
matching the established upstream housekeeping pattern.
Rewrite patch160 accordingly.

